== Storyline notes ==

* '''The injury costs him.''' Stan's knee gave out on the chokeslam lift — the same move that finished Honda on Day 1 and buckled him in Tokuyama. Nakamura's knee work was surgical and unsentimental, and the standing ovation for Stan as he was helped out was the emotional peak of the night. The medical question now hangs over every remaining Block A match: the giant is 1-2 with six matches left, and the knee will not hold for six more. See [[Big Stan knee injury (2026)]].
* '''Vance is alone at the top.''' 3-0, 6 points, no words since August 5. The Drill Driver out of the top-rope brainbuster counter is the tournament's most decisive finish so far. His remaining schedule: Kengo (Round 4, Ogasawara), Leoni (Round 5, Naruto), Nakamura (Round 6), Honda (Round 7), Maeda (Round 8), Morita (Round 9).
* '''The champion's homecoming.''' Leoni's win over Kengo was the expected result, delivered in the champion's home city with the ceremony whole — taualga, pate, namo. Kengo's kickout of the Spear at 2.4 was the fight left in him; the Namo Strike was the answer. The family war is over for now — Leoni is 2-0-1 and faces Maeda in Round 4 in Ogasawara.
* '''The Marauder problem.''' 2-1, and the block's honest wrestlers keep losing honest matches to him. Honda is the third opponent whose technical approach has failed against the no-sell. The Marauder's remaining schedule: Morita (Round 4, Ogasawara), Kawada (Round 5, Naruto), Leoni (Round 7, Anjo-Saikawa — the Spear kickout match), Stan (Round 8, Tsuda — forfeit), Nakamura (Round 9).
* '''The bottom is falling out for Morita.''' 0-3, and the flash cradle is no longer fooling anyone. His remaining schedule: the Marauder (Round 4), Nakamura (Round 5), Honda (Round 6), Stan (Round 7 — forfeit), Kengo (Round 8), Vance (Round 9). The Seigigun rising star is in free fall.

